  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1230 AM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nAn upper level shortwave trough looks to slide southeast through\nthe Plains and towards the forecast area on Wednesday, with an\nassociated cold front pushing through. There's still model\ndiscrepancies regarding timing and potency of this system,\nhowever a drier airmass looks to dominate for much of the\narea as the frontal boundary pushes through, keeping things \nmostly dry. The exception lies in the east/northeast portion of \nthe CWA, where better forcing and moisture exists, resulting in \nbetter precipitation chances (20-30%) and a few rumbles of \nthunder during the afternoon into the overnight hours.\n\nThe timing of the frontal passage will play a large role in\nWednesday's temperatures, however as of right now, highs look to\nonce again be in the mid 60s to low 70s for most ahead of the\ncold front.\n\nBehind this system, cooler air will filter in, dropping\ntemperatures a few degrees below normal in the 50s on Thursday,\nand the upper 40s to low 50s on Friday. The overnights will be\nchilly, with many locations dropping below freezing in the mid\n20s to mid 30s Thursday and Friday nights.",
